From 425cee1a40c02108c856b06172df260bcd40af77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:54:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: name a refused block-ack sub-frame by its
 refusing gate

The data receive refusal record (0288) names the first descriptor or
header field that differs from the admitted shape. Its status rung
compares the status word with 0xc000, the non-aggregated shape, while
the check itself has admitted block-ack sub-frames since 0319. Every
refused sub-frame therefore reads field=prefix whatever refused it:
boot AD's 341 refusals all read field=prefix with pn=lower, and the
PN was the cause.

The status rung now asks the check's own status predicate,
mt6797_ccmp_rx_status_ok(), so the ladder names the gate that refused
the frame: pn for a sub-frame whose PN is not above its TID's counter.
Without CONFIG_MT6797_RX_AMPDU the predicate is status == 0xc000 and
the record is unchanged. The status= bit names still list every bit
that differs from 0xc000.

Diagnostic only: no admission changes.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
index bfa777618..54a95851c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
@@ -855,6 +855,8 @@ static bool mt6797_ccmp_llc_mismatch(struct mt6797_mac *mac, size_t bytes)
  * word's bits that differ from the admitted 0xc000 are named as the pinned
  * nic_rx.h names them (0290). The PN's order is against the counter of the
  * frame's own TID in the context its WLAN index selects, both named (0292).
+ * The status rung is the check's own status gate, so a block-ack
+ * sub-frame the gate admits is named by the gate that refused it (0320).
  */
 static void mt6797_ccmp_rx_refused(struct mt6797_mac *mac, size_t bytes)
 {
@@ -916,7 +918,7 @@ static void mt6797_ccmp_rx_refused(struct mt6797_mac *mac, size_t bytes)
 		(p[6] & 0xbf) != 0x8e ? "layout" :
 		p[8] != 1 && p[8] != 2 ? "wlan-index" :
 		(p[9] & 0xf0) != 0x40 ? "cipher" :
-		mt6797_join_le16(p + 10) != 0xc000 ? "prefix" :
+		!mt6797_ccmp_rx_status_ok(mt6797_join_le16(p + 10)) ? "prefix" :
 		(groups & 9) != 9 ? "groups" :
 		(fc & ~(0x2800U | MT6797_CCMP_RX_QOS_BIT)) != 0x4208 ? "frame-control" :
 		((fc & 0x0080) ? (qos & ~0x000fU) || (qos & 15) != (p[9] & 15) :
-- 
